# CIS*2750 Assignment 3 - Testing Checklist


### 1. DB Login View (10 marks)

- User can enter all credentials
- Successfully establishes a connection to the database using the entered credentials
- Displays an error if the DB connection fails (e.g., incorrect credentials)
- Ensures tables in the database are created (only if they don't already exist)

### 2 Main View (30 marks)

- Displays all required details in a table format as specified in Module 1
- Does not display invalid files
- Files are clickable
- Correctly updates when a file is modified or created
- The database tables are populated correctly with file information
- Exits the program properly

### 3. Card Detail View (30 marks)

- Displays correct information for the selected file
- Information can be modified as stated in Module 1
- Changes are reflected on both the disk and in the database tables
- Exits back to the main view correctly

### 4. Create vCard (10 marks)

- Creates a new Card object and saves it to the vCard file
- User can input all details via forms
- Validates user input to prevent creating invalid vCard files
- Updates the database with the new vCard file

### 5. DB View (20 marks)

- Runs the two required queries
- Correctly displays information stored in the database tables
- Exits back to the main view correctly

### 6. Code Compilation:
  - Ensure your code compiles successfully using the provided Makefile
  - The Makefile should create a shared library (.so file) that will be used by `A3main.py`
  - Your code must run inside the Docker container provided for grading
  - Verify that everything works as expected within the container

### 7. Clean up:
  - Delete your compiled shared library (.so file) before submission
  - Recompile the shared library using your Makefile
  - Test the full application to ensure all functionality is working in the Docker container

Thank you!!
